## Materials and Methods
Fly stocks and hemocyte counting. Unless otherwise stated, all fly stocks were maintained at $25^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ on standard medium, and genotypes were verified with marked balancer chromosomes. For wasp infection, second instar larvae were submitted to egg-laying by $L$ boulardi for $2{\scriptstyle-4}\ \mathrm{~h~}$ , then allowed to develop at the appropriate temperature and analysed 24 or $^\mathrm{48h}$ later. Hemocyte observation and counting, and lacZ staining of lamellocytes, were as previously described (Braun et al. 1997; Duvic et al. 2002).
Transgenic constructs and flies. The srpD-Gal4 transgene: A distal promoter fragment, between 8.8 and $\bar{6}\ \mathrm{\kb}$ upstream of the srp transcription start site and a 340-bp fragment overlapping this site were amplified by PCR using $5^{\prime}$ -GCTAGCGACGCGTGATGCAACTTAATCAA- ${\cdot}3^{\prime}$ and $5^{\prime}$ -CTGCAGTTTATGAATGGAAGACGCGGACG$3^{\prime}$ primers, and $5^{\prime}$ -CTGCAGACGGCCAAGTCCAACAACAACAA- ${\cdot}3^{\prime}$ and $5^{\prime}$ -GGATCCCTGTTGCTGCTGTAACTGTTGAT- ${\cdot}3^{\prime}$ primers, respectively, then fused before subcloning upstream of the Gal4 coding sequence in a pCaSpeR vector. Transgenic lines were obtained by standard procedures. Because they are embryonic-lethal at $25^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , the srpD-Gal4/UAS-col animals were kept at $18~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ before shifting to $25~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ at the second larval instar.
Immunostaining and in situ hybridisation. Immunostaining and in situ hybridisation of larval lymph glands and embryos were performed as in Crozatier and Vincent (1999) using rabbit anti-Col (1:250), rat anti-Ser (gift from K. Irvine; 1:500), mouse anti- $\upbeta$ - galactosidase (Promega, Madison, Wisconsin, United States; 1:1000), mouse lamellocyte-specific L1 (gift from I. Ando; 1:10), and guineapig anti-Odd-skipped (gift from J. B. Skeath; 1:100). Peroxidase and Alexa Fluor 546 or 488 labelled secondary antibodies (Molecular Probes, Eugene, Oregon, United States) were used at a 1:500 dilution. In some cases, lymph glands were incubated for $30~\mathrm{min}$ at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in a propidium iodide solution in the presence of RNase. Mounting in Vectashield medium (Vector Laboratories, Burlingame, California, United States) preceded observation by confocal microscopy (Zeiss LSM 510 [Zeiss, Oberkochen, Germany] and Leica SP2 [Leica, Wetzlar, Germany]). Single-stranded digoxigenin-labelled RNA
